# Ignore everything
*

# Allow selected directories and everything inside
!maps/
!maps/**

!figures/
!figures/**

!assets/
!assets/**

!logos/
!logos/**

!theme/
!theme/**

!scripts/
!scripts/**

!.vscode/
!.vscode/**

!data/
!data/**

# .gpkg files carry real per-building data far richer than the JSON/GeoJSON
# files (many more experiment/model columns) and aren't fetched by any map
# app at runtime (confirmed: nothing under maps/ references *.gpkg) — pure
# unused source/intermediate data, so excluded outright rather than
# obscured. (data/unified/naco.gpkg also exceeds GitHub's 100MB push limit
# regardless.)
data/unified/*.gpkg
data/structural_system/*/buildings.gpkg

# The REAL per-building survey data (structural system, height, roof
# material, year, etc.) — data/ itself only ever holds the obscured/
# perturbed version (see scripts/obscure_building_data.py) that's safe to
# publish; this local-only backup must never be tracked. Already caught by
# the leading "ignore everything" pattern above (this repo has no `!data_original/`
# allowlist entry), but listed explicitly so it stays excluded even if that
# changes later.
data_original/
data_original/**

# The obscuring method itself stays private too (knowing exactly how
# data/ was perturbed makes it easier to reason backward toward the real
# values it was perturbed from).
scripts/obscure_building_data.py

# Python bytecode cache — no reason to ever track this.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/**

# Allow selected root files
!.gitignore
!presentation.md
!presentation.static.md
!index.html
!maps_manifest.json
!check_large_files.py
!export.md
!Urena_Pliego_et_al.pdf